    {
      "path": "README.md",
      "entry": "生命依存推进：[保留组织与变化中的生命活动](theories/shengsheng-buxi-generative-existence/unified-2026-10-05/LIVING-DEPENDENCIES.md#retained-organization-through-a-changing-transition)把已有共同分配证明连接到实际营养转变的证据，区分原有条件的持续作用与变化后的功能要求。此次为对应研究，无新定理或重复编译；下一检验是独立确定既有供给能否支持指定接续。 / Living-dependency development connects the existing allocation proofs to evidence from a measured nutrient transition, distinguishing retained conditions from changed functional requirements. This correspondence study adds no theorem or compilation; the next test independently assesses inherited provision for specified continuation.",
      "entry_sha256": "0edbc252854b04e2131576c117ef0bc2e473a58542b617551cd5b8db88a411d0"
    },
    {
      "path": "RESEARCH.md",
      "entry": "**Living dependencies: retained provision through a changing transition, 8 October 2026.** [The new correspondence round](_process/research/2026-10-05-generative-foundation-review/root-foundation/LIVING-DEPENDENCY-INTEGRATION.md#10-retained-organization-through-a-changing-living-transition) examines a measured bacterial nutrient transition, distinguishing causal initial-condition evidence, later reallocation and retained material. Its affirmative argument, independent review and formal-correspondence audit preserve alternative routes, measurement units and model-dependent interpretation. **No new theorem, numerical fit or Lean rerun:** the preceding 16-theorem allocation result retains its untimed scope. A generic occupation bound was deferred because it would not identify the missing biological relationship. The [current formulation](theories/shengsheng-buxi-generative-existence/unified-2026-10-05/LIVING-DEPENDENCIES.md) fixes four coverage obligations. **Next:** independently bound inherited provision against a specified continuing phenotype, including successful retention and recruitment alternatives. The broader living goal remains active.",
      "entry_sha256": "91b718c13fd3b3ce8e4ec6117e5421a8ba8638cb0304ac951ad2f4b156d9947a"
    },
    {
      "path": "theories/shengsheng-buxi-generative-existence/README.md",
      "entry": "**Living dependencies, extended 8 October 2026; current directed focus.** [The current formulation](unified-2026-10-05/LIVING-DEPENDENCIES.md) connects transport, recovery, organizing structures and joint participation. [The latest correspondence study](../../_process/research/2026-10-05-generative-foundation-review/root-foundation/LIVING-DEPENDENCY-INTEGRATION.md#10-retained-organization-through-a-changing-living-transition) tests retained provision through a measured nutrient transition and distinguishes changed requirements from disappearance of old material. It adds no theorem or Lean rerun; the preceding 16-theorem allocation result remains untimed. The next test independently bounds inherited provision for a specified phenotype, preserving adequate alternatives. Broader living coverage and ethical authority retain their separate scopes.",
      "entry_sha256": "fd059b7849f5035f61e73e37fcc9c4976572170247fbf088bf1a6938643f1b33"
    },
    {
      "path": "theories/shengsheng-buxi-generative-existence/unified-2026-10-05/GENERATIVE-GROUNDING.md",
      "entry": "**Living dependencies as the current directed focus, extended 8 October 2026:** [Ren selects this connection](../../../sources/15-codex-theory-conversations/2026-10-07-living-dependencies-current-goal.md). [The current derivation](LIVING-DEPENDENCIES.md) connects maintenance, recovery, organization and joint allocation to a measured changing transition. New primary-source assessment and independent review refine how retained provision, changed participation and later functioning are identified. No new theorem or compilation is claimed; the preceding allocation proof retains its conditional untimed scope. The next test compares independently warranted inherited provision with a specified continuing phenotype, including alternatives. The four coverage requirements and the broader living goal remain open; other authorized research retains its scope.",
      "entry_sha256": "9d9d927a50e8bea9a0316b2836adf359a503728c707df914145ccbc76285b40e"
    },
    {
      "path": "theories/shengsheng-buxi-generative-existence/unified-2026-10-05/UNIFIED-ETHICAL-GROUNDING.md",
      "entry": "**Living-dependency connection advanced, extended 8 October 2026.** Under [Ren's living focus](../../../sources/15-codex-theory-conversations/2026-10-07-living-dependencies-current-goal.md), [the current account](LIVING-DEPENDENCIES.md) now tests retained provision and changing requirements through a measured biological transition. Evidence and independent review distinguish causal contribution, ordinary coordinated experiments and stronger exclusive-necessity or formal-refinement claims. This explanatory advance adds no new theorem or ethical authority; existing proofs keep their validation scope. Independently bounding inherited provision for a specified continuing phenotype, and broader living coverage, remain the next work.",
      "entry_sha256": "cead78f601c7b526bb82aa49f97d9eabeb1de8e28e8cfa318ccda2d62317f350"
    }
  ],
